The library's version script (versions.ldscript) ends in a "local: *", and
it travels in linkopts to every binary that links libnuma. lld then keeps
every other symbol of the executable out of .dynsym even with a
--dynamic-list, so a dynamically linked executable with clang's static ASan
runtime cannot export the runtime's malloc and free to libc.so (glibc's own
getline() then mallocs from the real malloc and ASan reports a bad free,
step 7.1). The version tags mean nothing in a static link of libnuma.

--- a/BUILD.bazel	2026-10-07 02:31:40.985091473 -0700
+++ b/BUILD.bazel	2026-10-07 02:31:40.995091612 -0700
@@ -78,11 +78,9 @@
         "numacompat1.h",
         "numaif.h",
     ],
-    additional_linker_inputs = ["versions.ldscript"],
     copts = COMMON_COPTS,
     includes = ["."],
     linkopts = [
-        "-Wl,--version-script=$(location versions.ldscript)",
         "-Wl,-init,numa_init",
         "-Wl,-fini,numa_fini",
     ],
